-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: working out a deadline that stops at a limit. Run
-- with --max-steps 500, `count` 200000 takes more steps than that: l4 explore
-- stops and says so (exit 1), since a graph without the tick would be missing
-- positions; l4 lts lists the deadline as not known, with the evaluator's
-- words.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`count` n MEANS IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 10 ELSE `count` (n MINUS 1)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`slow` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `count` 200000 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
